   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/review-1247-opus, round 1): APPROVE** — head 122738fd\n\nI found no behaviour change.\n- `isListed` was `{ true }` for every case, so dropping its guards in `isOn`, `set` and `listedFeatures` leaves every reader as it was. The readers checked: `ExperimentalSettings.isOn(_:in:)`, `ExperimentalSettingsView`, `DescribedFeatureRow`, `MPStorageSyncModel`, `ImageLoadingChoice`.\n- `ComposerToolStyle.current` was always `.pills`, so `diameter = inCard ? chip : cell` matches the old expression at every caller: `ComposerControlRow.button`, `ComposerHeader.buttonSize`, `FloatingComposerButtons`.\n- No `switch` over `HapticFeedback.Kind` remains apart from `play`.\n- `TopicSource(mode: .flagsAndFavorites)` gives `.flagged` (`TopicSource.swift:66-68`), which is what the old constant held. `categoriesStartupSource` is unchanged.\n\nFindings:\n\n1. **Low**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Experimental/ExperimentalSettingsTests.swift:365`: the new `#expect(Set(listed) == Set(ExperimentalFeature.allCases))` cannot fail. `theme` is an exhaustive switch, `listedFeatures` filters by theme, and `listed` keeps every theme that has a feature, so together they always cover `allCases`. Scenario: add a case with any theme and this line stays green; only the hard-coded list on line 364 catches it. This is the kind of self-comparing test #1196 removes. Fix: delete the line. `groups.flatMap(\\.features) == allCases` (line 375) does check something (section order must match enum order), so keep it.\n2. **Detail**, PR body:\n   - \"`RootModel.swift:209`\" is line 207 at the head.\n   - \"The nine suites\" are ten since #1231 merged.\n   - The order note about #1231 (\"I merge `dev-swift` once #1231 lands\") is out of date: the merge is done.\n   - Add `Reviewer model:`.\n\n**Vérifié**\n- Diff `origin/dev-swift...122738fd`, all 28 files.\n- `git show --remerge-diff 122738fd~1` is empty.\n- SwiftLint on `App/SwiftHFR` and `App/SwiftHFRTests` in a throwaway worktree: exit 0. The worktree is removed.\n- `git grep` for `isListed|owningLot|isBuilt|ComposerToolStyle|favoritesStartupSource|.notification(` in App, docs, tooling and Packages: no hits.\n- Edits to LOT-123 and LOT-174 match the code.\n- #895 comment 6913715068 (REST): \"variant D (chips) kept as the default\", 2026-11-16.\n- `git merge-tree` of the head with #1240's head `afe800c7`: clean, no conflict.\n- App tests not run (Linux); the compile check is green on the head, as reported.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
